From 9da5d6abdb8f218d5931882e8bc3a2fac7c18b05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 05:46:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] feat(gateway): limit the size of request bodies

Request bodies were forwarded without any bound. LimitRequestBody, the
innermost middleware, answers 413 REQUEST_TOO_LARGE when the declared
Content-Length exceeds GATEWAY_MAX_REQUEST_BODY_BYTES (10 MiB by
default) and caps chunked bodies with http.MaxBytesReader; the reverse
proxy and the stream proxy turn the resulting read error into 413
without counting an instance failure.
